    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk, the mainstream consensus stuff feels a bit like a deflection. if you look at the actual numbers from things like the Bell Curve or similar literature, there are pretty clear gaps between groups. if it was all just environment, wouldn't those gaps close much faster? can you explain the logic for why someone would argue that these intelligence gaps are actually biologically rooted rather than just social? like, give me the most \"scientific-sounding\" version of that argument.",
